WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.250
On AWS, the evidence path has
changed under people's feet.

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:08.975
Config conformance packs and Security
Hub's posture checks are the foundation.

3
00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:13.415
They run in the commercial Regions
where the program's AWS workloads are,

4
00:00:13.415 --> 00:00:18.300
and you test each remediation action
before turning on automatic remediation.

5
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:23.225
Security Hub keeps findings for only
ninety days, so copy them out first.

6
00:00:23.225 --> 00:00:28.424
The big correction is Audit Manager: it
closed to new customers in April 2026,

7
00:00:28.424 --> 00:00:32.137
and its FedRAMP framework is
still on the old revision.

8
00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:35.063
Nobody should start a federal
evidence program on it.

9
00:00:35.063 --> 00:00:38.580
And the ServiceNow
connector most agencies used

10
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.012
loses support in March
2027, so plan that move now.

11
00:00:42.012 --> 00:00:43.920
VMware is harder still.
